@startuml
title ReLink Initial Connection Flow

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true

actor "Initiator\nClient A" as A
participant "A Local Crypto\nconnection_init_local\nconnection_encrypt" as ACrypto
participant "Caddy\nHTTPS / WSS edge" as Caddy
participant "Axum Router\nhandlers + WS endpoint" as Axum
participant "RendezvousService" as Rendezvous
database "Redis" as Redis
participant "PushHub" as PushHub
actor "Receiver\nClient B" as B
participant "B Local Crypto\nconnection_derive_keys\nconnection_encrypt/decrypt" as BCrypto
participant "WebRTC A" as WebRtcA
participant "WebRTC B" as WebRtcB
participant "STUN\ncoturn --stun-only" as Stun

== Phase 1: Link Provisioning ==

A -> ACrypto : Generate `rendezvous_id` + `secret`\nDerive `kSig`, `kMac`, `sas`
A -> Caddy : `POST /connection/init`\n`{ rendezvous_id_b64 }`
Caddy -> Axum : Reverse proxy request
Axum -> Rendezvous : `init_connection(rendezvous_id_b64)`
Rendezvous -> Redis : `SETEX sig:mailbox_meta:mailboxA`\n`DEL sig:mailbox_msgs:mailboxA`
Rendezvous -> Redis : `SETEX sig:rendezvous:{token} -> mailboxA`
Rendezvous --> Axum : `mailboxA`, `expires_at_epoch_ms`
Axum --> Caddy : `200 OK`
Caddy --> A : `mailboxA`, `expires_at_epoch_ms`

A -> Caddy : `GET /ws/:mailboxA` (upgrade)
Caddy -> Axum : Reverse proxy WS upgrade
Axum -> PushHub : subscribe `mailboxA`

A -> B : Share deep link out-of-band\n`/connection/join?token=<rendezvous_id>#<secret>`

== Phase 2: Join + Pairing ==

B -> BCrypto : Parse secret from URL fragment\nDerive `kSig`, `kMac`, `sas`
B -> Caddy : `POST /connection/join`\n`{ token_b64 }`
Caddy -> Axum : Reverse proxy request
Axum -> Rendezvous : `join_connection(token_b64)`
Rendezvous -> Redis : `GET sig:rendezvous:{token}`\nthen `DEL`
Rendezvous -> Redis : `GET sig:mailbox_meta:mailboxA`
Rendezvous -> Redis : Update `mailboxA.peer_mailbox_id = mailboxB`
Rendezvous -> Redis : `SETEX sig:mailbox_meta:mailboxB`
Rendezvous -> Redis : `RPUSH sig:mailbox_msgs:mailboxA`\njoin marker `{from_mailbox_id: mailboxB, ciphertext_b64: ""}`
Rendezvous --> Axum : `mailboxB`, `expires_at`, join marker
Axum -> PushHub : notify `mailboxA`
PushHub --> Axum : broadcast mailboxA event
Axum --> A : WS push join marker

note right of A
The blank `ciphertext_b64` join marker is what triggers
the "Incoming Connection" / "Accept" dialog in `InitiatorPage`.
end note

B -> Caddy : `GET /ws/:mailboxB` (upgrade)
Caddy -> Axum : Reverse proxy WS upgrade
Axum -> PushHub : subscribe `mailboxB`

B -> BCrypto : Encrypt `connect_request`
B -> Caddy : `POST /connection/send`\n`{ mailbox_id: mailboxB, ciphertext_b64 }`
Caddy -> Axum : Reverse proxy request
Axum -> Rendezvous : `send_message(mailboxB, ciphertext)`
Rendezvous -> Redis : `RPUSH sig:mailbox_msgs:mailboxA`
Axum -> PushHub : notify `mailboxA`
PushHub --> Axum : broadcast mailboxA event
Axum --> A : WS push encrypted `connect_request`

note right of A
`_handleIncomingSignal()` only handles `answer`, `ice`,
and `disconnect`, so this encrypted `connect_request`
is effectively ignored by the initiator parser.
end note

== Phase 3: SDP Exchange ==

A -> WebRtcA : User accepts dialog\nInitialize peer connection\nCreate SDP offer
WebRtcA -> ACrypto : Encrypt offer
A -> Caddy : `POST /connection/send`\n`mailboxA + encrypted offer`
Caddy -> Axum : Reverse proxy request
Axum -> Rendezvous : `send_message(mailboxA, offer)`
Rendezvous -> Redis : `RPUSH sig:mailbox_msgs:mailboxB`
Axum -> PushHub : notify `mailboxB`
PushHub --> Axum : broadcast mailboxB event
Axum --> B : WS push encrypted offer

B -> BCrypto : Decrypt offer
BCrypto --> B : JSON signaling payload
B -> WebRtcB : `setRemoteDescription(offer)`\nCreate SDP answer
WebRtcB -> BCrypto : Encrypt answer
B -> Caddy : `POST /connection/send`\n`mailboxB + encrypted answer`
Caddy -> Axum : Reverse proxy request
Axum -> Rendezvous : `send_message(mailboxB, answer)`
Rendezvous -> Redis : `RPUSH sig:mailbox_msgs:mailboxA`
Axum -> PushHub : notify `mailboxA`
PushHub --> Axum : broadcast mailboxA event
Axum --> A : WS push encrypted answer

A -> ACrypto : Decrypt answer
ACrypto --> A : JSON signaling payload
A -> WebRtcA : `setRemoteAnswer(answer)`

== Phase 4: ICE + Transport Establishment ==

par Initiator ICE
  WebRtcA -> Stun : STUN binding requests
  Stun --> WebRtcA : server-reflexive candidates
  WebRtcA -> ACrypto : Encrypt trickle ICE
  A -> Caddy : `POST /connection/send`\n`mailboxA + encrypted ice`
  Caddy -> Axum : Reverse proxy request
  Axum -> Rendezvous : `send_message(mailboxA, ice)`
  Rendezvous -> Redis : `RPUSH sig:mailbox_msgs:mailboxB`
  Axum -> PushHub : notify `mailboxB`
  PushHub --> Axum : broadcast mailboxB event
  Axum --> B : WS push encrypted ICE
  B -> BCrypto : Decrypt ICE
  B -> WebRtcB : `addIceCandidate(...)`
else Receiver ICE
  WebRtcB -> Stun : STUN binding requests
  Stun --> WebRtcB : server-reflexive candidates
  WebRtcB -> BCrypto : Encrypt trickle ICE
  B -> Caddy : `POST /connection/send`\n`mailboxB + encrypted ice`
  Caddy -> Axum : Reverse proxy request
  Axum -> Rendezvous : `send_message(mailboxB, ice)`
  Rendezvous -> Redis : `RPUSH sig:mailbox_msgs:mailboxA`
  Axum -> PushHub : notify `mailboxA`
  PushHub --> Axum : broadcast mailboxA event
  Axum --> A : WS push encrypted ICE
  A -> ACrypto : Decrypt ICE
  A -> WebRtcA : `addIceCandidate(...)`
end

WebRtcA <-> WebRtcB : DTLS handshake\nSRTP / SCTP setup
WebRtcA <-> WebRtcB : Direct P2P channels established

note over A,B
After `RTCPeerConnectionStateConnected`, both pages call
`_closeSignalingAfterConnect()`, close mailbox signaling,
and move late control / ICE over the direct WebRTC data channels.
end note

note over A,Axum
`ConnectionService.subscribeMailbox()` also performs
`POST /connection/recv` after WS connect to backfill missed messages.
That recovery path exists in the current implementation but is not
the primary happy-path signal carrier shown above.
end note

@enduml
